  "id": "social-stimulus",
  "term": "social stimulus",
  "definition": "A social stimulus is something a person perceives that carries social cues or information, such as signals available in biological motion. In this source, social stimuli are contrasted with non-social stimuli because they are relevant to social recognition and can automatically draw attention.",
